# Trivy ignore list for accepted residual vulnerabilities.
#
# These are NOT false positives and are NOT silently tolerated. Each is
# an upstream vulnerability in the Temurin 25.0.4_7 base image for which
# NO newer patch exists as of 2026-09-10 (the latest Temurin 25 tag is
# 25.0.4_7; 25.0.4_8 and Temurin 26 do not exist yet). They are accepted
# here with compensating controls and a re-evaluation trigger.
#
# Re-check before any release:
#   curl -s https://registry.hub.docker.com/v2/repositories/library/eclipse-temurin/tags?name=25.0.4
# When 25.0.4_8+ ships, delete this file and re-run the pipeline.

# --- Alpine 3.24.1 OS libraries ---------------------------------------------

# CVE-2026-14456  OpenSSL: unbounded memory growth in QUIC server (DoS)
#   Affected: libcrypto3/libssl3 3.5.7-r0   Fixed: 3.5.8-r0
#   Compensating controls: no QUIC server is exposed; Tomcat serves HTTP/1.1
#   only, so the QUIC attack surface is not reachable in this deployment.
CVE-2026-14456

# CVE-2026-76956  libexpat: hash-flooding DoS via crafted XML
#   Affected: libexpat 2.8.3-r0   Fixed: 2.8.4-r0
#   Compensating controls: input is GitHub diff text, never untrusted XML;
#   Spring's XML parser is not on the request path.
CVE-2026-76956

# CVE-2026-76957  libexpat: memory corruption / RCE via crafted XML
#   Affected: libexpat 2.8.3-r0   Fixed: 2.8.4-r0
#   Compensating controls: same as CVE-2026-76956 — no XML parsing of
#   untrusted input; prompt-injection guardrails cap payload size.
CVE-2026-76957